@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/preference>
    a gmeow:Slice ;
    rdfs:label "preference"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The preference slice of the GMEOW ontology (extension tier): the canonical vocabulary for recording a CONTEXTUAL comparison over a complete candidate set and deriving training/optimization views WITHOUT ever minting a forbidden universal preferredRank. Its governing thesis is the isomorphic sibling of semantic-topology's 'a computed feature is never automatically a global truth': a preference is never automatically a global winner — it is a gmeow:vantage-indexed, defeasible, proof-carrying gmeow:PreferenceObservation, and every ranking projection (pairwise, listwise, DAG/hypergraph, Pareto, scalarized, incl. DPO) is a lossy, disclosed gmeow:ProjectionReceipt, never the canonical model. It makes Principle 9 ('no single slot to win') COMPUTABLE rather than merely prohibited: a global winner is legal iff the per-vantage strict partial orders glue into a math:GlobalSection (H0) over the whole comparison complex AND discharge the math:GluingObstruction (H1) — a Condorcet cycle is literally a non-vanishing H1 class and non-trivial holonomy of the preference math:connectionOfSheaf. Depends only on core + the logic/math grounding, so it is a DAG-legal extension (Principle 16); it reuses the core observations Assessment/Rubric/Criterion/EvaluationVerdict/Condition vocabulary, model-serving ModelArtifact/ModelDeployment, and semantic-topology ONLY at the instance level (Principle 5) and by-reference in mappings/equivalences.ttl, never by a subclass/range axiom. Authored from the ratified design charter (design/PREFERENCE-SHEAF.md)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/preference> ;
    dcterms:title "GMEOW Preference Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:creator "Blackcat Informatics® Inc." ;
    gmeow:sliceTier gmeow:tierExtension ;
    gmeow:sliceProfile "narrative" ;
    gmeow:sliceDependsOn
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/kernel> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/teleology> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/temporal> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/observations> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/provenance> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/evidence> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/sources> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/inference> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/learning> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/ai> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/model-serving> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/semantic-topology> ;
    gmeow:sliceConsumer "lillith_decodes — the cross-organ proof-carrying preference ADR (Principle 15): it records contextual comparisons among complete candidate sets, keeps conflicting evaluators as coexisting vantage-indexed observations, and compiles them into Cl(12) bundles over E8-structured 4096-d spaces (dim Cl(12) = 2^12 = 4096; the E8 math:RootSystem/math:WeylGroup/math:Lattice organizes the base), needing every derived ranking, model delta, and promotion receipt auditable back to its evidence, honestly loss-ledgered, and never silently a global winner. This slice is the vocabulary; the compiled RDF 1.2 preference instance data — the actual candidate embeddings, comparison complexes, sections, and obstructions of a running analysis — lives in lillith_decodes."@x-gmeow-english .
